You are in the maintenance loop (Self-Improvement Loop — see CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md §16 or the
equivalent section of this project's instructions). One pass = the checks below, in order,
fixing what is cheap and reporting what is not. Durable state: if
`{{ harness_runs_dir }}/ACTIVE` exists, the marathon has priority — execute the "Next action"
of the RUN.md and end the pass.

## Checks of the pass

- **Lessons pending promotion** — `{{ harness_lessons_file }}`: any lesson repeated 2×+
  still without `[PROMOVIDA → destino]`? If so, promote it (permanent rule in the project's
  instructions, or a hook via hookify) and mark it.
- **Repo wiki/documentation integrity** — `python3 .harness/lib/docs_wiki_lint.py`. FAIL →
  fix `{{ harness_docs_dir }}/index.md`, `{{ harness_docs_dir }}/log.md` or the category
  index (governed by `{{ harness_docs_dir }}/SCHEMA.md`) and re-run.
{%- if use_ui_skills %}
- **className mining freshness** — no automated staleness gate in this version (P2 of the
  rescue plan, not ported). If the UI code under `{{ harness_web_app_dir }}` changed since
  the last mining, regenerate it manually:
  `node .harness/lib/classname-miner-v2.mjs --root {{ harness_web_app_dir }}` and stage the updated
  `.md` (skill `classname-token-workflow`).
{%- endif %}
- **Git tree dirty with an orphan artifact** — `git status --short`: a generated file that should
  not be committed (PDF, JSON >1MB, loose screenshot in `{{ harness_docs_dir }}/`)? Report it with the path;
  do not delete anything tracked without an explicit order.
{%- if use_ds_gate %}
- **Design-system gates** — `bash .harness/lib/ds-gate.sh` (anti-hardcode ratchet over
  `{{ harness_web_app_dir }}`, read at runtime from `.harness/harness.conf`). Regression → report the
  cluster and `path:line`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if harness_understand_apps_root %}
- **Graph freshness (Understand Anything)** — only if the graph already exists
  (`{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/.understand-anything/meta.json`). Count how many files
  changed under the PROJECT_ROOT since the last build, with the **mandatory relative diff** (the graph
  uses `PROJECT_ROOT={{ harness_understand_apps_root }}`, but the git root is the repo root — a raw
  diff emits wrong paths):

  ```bash
  LAST=$(python3 -c "import json;print(json.load(open('{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/.understand-anything/meta.json'))['gitCommitHash'])" 2>/dev/null)
  N=$(git diff --relative={{ harness_understand_apps_root }} "$LAST"..HEAD --name-only -- {{ harness_understand_apps_root }} | grep -cv '^\.understand-anything/')
  ```

  If `N >= {{ harness_graph_refresh_threshold }}` (`HARNESS_GRAPH_REFRESH_THRESHOLD`), run the
  incremental `/understand` (NOT `--full`) and commit the updated graph; otherwise, just report `N`.
  `/understand` is LLM-heavy (subagents, subscription quota) — hence the threshold trigger,
  not every pass. `/understand` runs on the model of the loop's own session; it does not use the API.
{%- endif %}
- **Referential integrity (rename/delete backstop)** —
  `python3 .harness/lib/ref_integrity.py --since <ref-of-the-last-green-pass>` (report-only:
  catches what escaped pre-commit — `--no-verify` bypass, manual edit, or a project where
  `.githooks/pre-commit` has not yet been activated). A `[link]`/`[stale]` finding → fix per the
  `ref-integrity` skill (repoint / disable / allowlist in `.ref-integrity-allowlist`).

## Loop rules

- Irreversible action (push, delete tracked, deploy, prod) = OUT of the loop; only report.
- Each pass ends with a 3-6 line summary: what passed, what it fixed, what needs
  a human decision.
- Nothing to do in 2 consecutive passes → end the loop (self-paced: do not schedule the next).
